  "display_text": "Question scope: NAB / FY2025\n\nNAB's credit impairment charge was 728 AUD million for the year ended 30 September 2024 (cash basis, continuing operations). This shows the expense magnitude; the signed source value remains available in the workings. NAB's credit impairment charge was 833 AUD million for the year ended 30 September 2025 (cash basis, continuing operations). This shows the expense magnitude; the signed source value remains available in the workings. [NAB FY2025 Full Year Results, PDF page 13]\n\nFor NAB credit impairment charge, the comparison from 2024-09-30 to 2025-09-30 gives an increase of 105 AUD million. The relative change is +14.42% (rounded). [NAB FY2025 Full Year Results, PDF page 13]\n\nNAB FY2025 reports: \"Credit impairment charge increased by $105 million or 14.4%, driven by a higher level of individually assessed credit impairment charge primarily in Corporate and Institutional Banking. This was partially offset by a lower level of collective credit impairment charge.\" [NAB FY2025 Full Year Results, PDF page 14]\n\nThese are selected report passages, not an exhaustive review or a newly inferred causal explanation. Quoted amounts are not new calculations.\nCBA and NAB prose search includes all six reports' extractable text. Retrieved passages are not an exhaustive review; unvalidated tables and image-only content are not calculation-ready.\nCited passages support only what the source explicitly discloses. Quoted figures are not newly calculated results or a complete review of every report.\nThe movement is checked first; explanatory passages are restricted to its source report(s). Different reporting bases are not interchangeable.\nFor the stated FY2025 movement, checking FY2024 to FY2025 on a compatible reporting basis."
